{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And He said, I will cause all My goodness to pass, etc.</b> The hour has arrived that you shall see in My glory what I permit you to see — for I wish and need to teach you the order of prayer: that when you need to seek mercy for Israel, you recall to Me the merit of the fathers. For you might think that if the merit of the fathers is exhausted there is no further hope — so I will cause all the measure of My goodness to pass before you upon the rock while you stand in the cleft." "<b>And I will call in the name of YHWH before you.</b> To teach you the order of requesting mercy even if the merit of the fathers is exhausted. And according to this order that you see Me — wrapped and reciting the thirteen attributes — so shall you teach Israel to do, and by their reciting before Me 'compassionate and gracious' they will be answered — for My compassions do not cease." "<b>And I will be gracious to whom I will be gracious.</b> At those times when I wish to be gracious." "<b>And I will show mercy.</b> At a time when I wish to show mercy. Up to here He promised him only: sometimes I will answer and sometimes I will not answer. But at the time of the deed He said to him, ״Behold, I am making a covenant״ (Exodus 34) — He promised him that they do not return empty."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:26.893009403Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}